{
  "requirement": "During one call to `verify`, direct reads by the criterion and\nreads served by the SDK's agent tools record inputs in the same\n`ValidationContext`. For example, if criterion code reads a test and the agent\nthen reads its helper, both node fingerprints accompany the returned answer.\nA subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural check finds no gap. I did not assess tests or runtime behavior.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Direct criterion reads and agent-tool reads record into the same `ValidationContext` during one `verify` call.\n2. Both the criterion's reads and the agent's reads end up in the returned answer's dependencies.\n3. A later verification starts with an empty dependency list.\n\n**Direct reads**\n- `ValidationContext` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs` holds a single `observations` mutex-guarded `Vec<Dependency<..>>`.\n- `read`, `read_snapshot` and `outgoing_edges` all record into that vector through `record_read` and `observe_edges`.\n\n**Agent reads use the same context**\n- `Ask::execute` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs` (`impl[Ask<..>]#2/fn[execute]`) passes `self.ctx` itself to `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`. It does not pass a copy.\n- `ToolAgent::run` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs` stores that `&ValidationContext` as `GraphSession.inspection`.\n- `GraphSession::dispatch` serves `read_node` and `outgoing_edges` by calling `prepare_read` and `prepare_edges` on `self.inspection`. It queues the observations in `pending`. Other tools' dependencies are queued the same way.\n- `GraphSession::delivered` drains `pending` into `self.inspection.record_read` and `observe_edges`, which write to the same `observations` vector.\n- `converse` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent.rs` calls `session.delivered()` after each delivered response. Agent reads are therefore recorded in the shared context only once their results are delivered.\n\n**Both fingerprints accompany the answer**\n- `execute_with_context` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs` runs the criterion with one `ctx`. It returns `dependencies: ctx.dependencies()`, which clones the shared `observations`.\n- A criterion read and a later agent read of a helper both land in that one vector, so both fingerprints are returned. `record_read` and `observe_edges_by` skip an entry only when an identical one is already present.\n\n**Fresh list per verification**\n- `verify` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs` builds a new `ValidationContext::new(domain, criterion.source_node_id())` on every call.\n- `ValidationContext::configured` initializes `observations: Default::default()`, so each verification starts empty.\n\n**Impl markings**\nThe `{impl}` markings on `fn[run]`, `struct[GraphSession]`, `fn[dispatch]`, `fn[delivered]` and `Ask::execute` each correspond to one of these structural links. The shared context is passed through `run` and `GraphSession`, observations are queued in `dispatch`, and they are imported in `delivered`. No unacknowledged structural gaps remain, and there are no FIXME acknowledgments.",
  "references": "2c35862fa48dbc05e8825f322f614b0f35937ab779b0239d61752080a67691e4",
